        <briefdescription>
<para>Evaluates a condition and reports the result. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expr_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the custom expression.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Constraints</title><para>Enabled only if <computeroutput>Expr_T</computeroutput> is a framework expression type or is contextually convertible to <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput>, including by an <computeroutput>explicit operator bool</computeroutput> (enforced via a C++20 <computeroutput>requires</computeroutput> clause, with <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1checkable" kindref="compound">extension::checkable</ref></computeroutput>).</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>expr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Logical expression to evaluate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sl</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional source location, defaulting to the current line. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>result</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The check result, a temporary created by the caller as the default argument, which the applications do not pass; it is destroyed at the end of the statement. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A reference to the check result, to which optional messages can be appended with <computeroutput>operator&lt;&lt;</computeroutput>; the check is reported when it is destroyed, at the end of the statement, so the result cannot be kept in a variable.</para>
</simplesect>
Initialises the <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1check__result" kindref="compound">detail::check_result</ref></computeroutput> received as the last argument, a temporary created by the caller, with the kind <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a0726a1bc3b6f16245cb8a4b42fe0e70cae15c5d274bf9fa6571890c731d88bc37" kindref="member">detail::check_kind::expectation</ref></computeroutput>, and returns a reference to it. The check result evaluates the condition when initialised, and records a pass or fail when it is destroyed, at the end of the expression statement.</para>
<para>Stops the compilation with the message of the <computeroutput>static_assert</computeroutput>, which states what <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-expectations_1ga6db7427ada09e476aec67306ca5c0b74" kindref="member">expect()</ref></computeroutput> takes. The condition of the <computeroutput>static_assert</computeroutput> depends on the type, so it is evaluated only when the function is selected.</para>
<para>Deprecated; the check is the same as that of <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-expectations_1ga6db7427ada09e476aec67306ca5c0b74" kindref="member">expect()</ref></computeroutput>, for the arguments that are always true. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
